    [
     1,
     "\r\n  \r\n    \r\n  \r\n  <div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\">\r\n    Thank you, I was after something slightly different- I wanted to\r\n    apply a function to the variable names only, and was sort of looking\r\n    to do it with dplyr verbs <br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    However Dennis Murphy kindly provided the following solution, using\r\n    only base R functions:<br>\r\n    <pre><big>names(toy_df) &lt;- tolower(names(toy_df))\r\n</big></pre>\r\n    <blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"color:#000000\">\r\n      <pre><big>names(toy_df)\r\n</big></pre>\r\n    </blockquote>\r\n    <pre><big>[1] &quot;city&quot;  &quot;state&quot;\r\n</big></pre></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\">\r\n    <br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    <div>On 3/5/15 7:38 PM, patrick kilduff\r\n      wrote:<br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n      <div style=\"color:#000;background-color:#fff;font-family:HelveticaNeue,Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">\r\n        <div>Hi,</div>\r\n        <div><br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div dir=\"ltr\">Does this do\r\n          what you want? (I&#39;m not clear at to what the &quot;batches&quot; are) <br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div dir=\"ltr\"><br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div dir=\"ltr\">toy_df &lt;-\r\n          data.frame(City = c(&quot;Little Rock&quot;, &quot;Chicago&quot;, &quot;Toledo&quot;), State\r\n          = c(&quot;Arkansas&quot;, &quot;Illinois&quot;, &quot;Ohio&quot;))<br>\r\n          <br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div dir=\"ltr\">sapply(toy_df,\r\n          tolower)<br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div dir=\"ltr\">#    \r\n          City          State     <br>\r\n          # [1,] &quot;little rock&quot; &quot;arkansas&quot;<br>\r\n          # [2,] &quot;chicago&quot;     &quot;illinois&quot;<br>\r\n          # [3,] &quot;toledo&quot;      &quot;ohio&quot; <br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div dir=\"ltr\"><span><br>\r\n          </span></div>\r\n        <div dir=\"ltr\"><span>-Patrick</span></div>\r\n        <div><br>\r\n          <br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div style=\"display:block\">\r\n          <div style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue,Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">\r\n            <div style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue,Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,Lucida Grande,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">\r\n              <div dir=\"ltr\"> <font face=\"Arial\" size=\"2\"> On Thursday,\r\n                  March 5, 2015 6:19 PM, ArjunaCap\r\n                  <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;mcaw...@greenstenergy.com&gt;</a> wrote:<br>\r\n                </font> </div>\r\n              <br>\r\n              <br>\r\n              <div>\r\n                <div>\r\n                  <div dir=\"ltr\">given the following df:\r\n                    <div><br>\r\n                    </div>\r\n                    <div>toy_df &lt;- data.frame(City = c(&quot;Little Rock&quot;,\r\n                      &quot;Chicago&quot;, &quot;Toledo&quot;), State = c(&quot;Arkansas&quot;,\r\n                      &quot;Illinois&quot;, &quot;Ohio&quot;))<br>\r\n                    </div>\r\n                    <div><br>\r\n                    </div>\r\n                    <div>if I wanted to rename the variables in a batch\r\n                      using a function (eg <font face=\"courier new,\r\n                        monospace\">tolower()</font>) , how could I do\r\n                      this?</div>\r\n                    <div><br>\r\n                    </div>\r\n                    <div>obviously, it&#39;s trivial to do so for the toy,\r\n                      but I need a generalizable way for a df with n\r\n                      variables.</div>\r\n                    <div><br>\r\n                    </div>\r\n                    <div>Thank you.</div>\r\n                  </div>\r\n                  -- <br>\r\n                  You received this message because you are subscribed\r\n                  to the Google Groups &quot;manipulatr&quot; group.<br>\r\n                  To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving\r\n                  emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\" href data-email-masked>manipulatr+...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n                  To post to this group, send email to <a rel=\"nofollow\" href data-email-masked>manip...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n                  Visit this group at <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/manipulatr\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/manipu